  "verbalization": "Fluoranthene is shown to have a target of Ataxin-2, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol, 5-Hydroxy-2-[2-hydroxy-4-[3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)tetrahydropyran-2-yl]oxy-phenyl]-8,8-dimethyl-3-(3-methylbut-2-enyl)pyrano[2,3-h]chromen-4-one, and Oleamide. All of these compounds share a common target, HUVEC, and are linked to Ataxin-2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Fluoranthene may interact with HUVEC. The evidence suggests that Fluoranthene may exert its effects through a mechanism involving Ataxin-2, which is a target of multiple compounds that are associated with HUVEC. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ataxin-2 and HUVEC supports a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of Fluoranthene's interaction with Ataxin-2 and its downstream effects on HUVEC remain to be fully elucidated.",
